# Reference Point — Subsection Title (`h3.title`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for a subsection headline (e.g. "AI + Human, One Chat", "Where the chatbot appears — and why"), match `h3.title` inside `.overview-sub-head.stack-16` or `header.hybrid-chat-head` in `#overview`, `#discovery`, or `#ai-layer`.

## Structure

```html
<!-- Pattern A — overview sub-head -->
<div class="overview-sub-head stack-16">
  <p class="eyebrow soft">Chatbot placement</p>
  <h3 class="title">Where the chatbot appears — and why</h3>
</div>

<!-- Pattern B — hybrid chat head (equivalent treatment) -->
<header class="hybrid-chat-head">
  <p class="eyebrow soft">Chatbot experience</p>
  <h3 class="title">AI + Human, One Chat</h3>
</header>
```

Pair with `p.eyebrow.soft` above — see `reference-point-eyebrow-soft.mdc`. Full block pattern in `reference-point-sub-head.mdc`.

## Visual spec

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `h3.title` inside `.overview-sub-head` or `.hybrid-chat-head` |
| Font | `var(--serif)` → Instrument Serif |
| Size | `var(--title-sm)` → **clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.25rem)** |
| Weight | **400** |
| Style | **Regular** (not italic); use `<em>` for phrase emphasis only |
| Color | `var(--ink-deep)` → **#1a1814** |
| Line-height | **1.1** |
| Max-width | **40rem** |
| Margin | **0** |

Scoped selectors (identical treatment):

```css
.overview-section .overview-sub-head h3.title,
#discovery .overview-sub-head h3.title,
#ai-layer .overview-sub-head h3.title,
.hybrid-chat-head h3.title,
#guardrails > .stack-32 > h3.title
```

Parent wrappers use `gap: 0.75rem` in `#ai-layer` / `#discovery` / `.hybrid-chat-head` (1rem in `#overview`). Full hybrid chat block: `reference-point-hybrid-chat-head.mdc`. Guardrails subsection heads (“Design Guardrails”, “System Guardrails…”) share the same `h3.title` treatment.

## vs other headlines

| Class / element | Use |
|-----------------|-----|
| **`h3.title` in `.overview-sub-head` or `.hybrid-chat-head`** | **Subsection head — regular serif, `--title-sm`** |
| `h3` in `.gap-card` | Card punchline — fully italic, `--h3`, `var(--ink)` |
| `.display` | Main section heads — largest, `--display` |
| `.col-title` | About column titles — italic, `--h3` |

## Do not

- Use `.display` or plain `h2` for subsection titles.
- Make the full line italic — only wrap emphasis phrases in `<em>`.
- Use `h3.title` without `.overview-sub-head` or `.hybrid-chat-head` wrapper — loses subsection context.
- Confuse with `.ai-touchpoint-head h4` — touchpoint card heads are 24px italic.
